{
 "text": "Reference\nCITY OF MANILA\nAGENCY ACTION PLAN AND STATUS of IMPLEMENTATION\nAudit Observations and Recommendations\nFor the Calendar Year 2024\nAs of August 31, 2025\nAudit Observations\nb.Cash Advances required for immediate liquidation\nand settlement totaling P106.136 million pertained to\naccounts of AOs who are already deceased, resigned,\nretired or separated from the City that have been\naged two months to 19 years, contrary to Section\n4.1.3 of COA Circular No. 97-002 dated February 10,\n1997; and\nc.Additional cash advances were granted to six AOs\ndespite non-liquidation or non-settlement of their\nprevious cash advances, which is contrary to Item\n4.1.2 of COA Circular No. 97-002, resulting in\ndifficulty of liquidation, improper/unmonitored\nutilization and accumulation of cash advances.\nThese circumstances resulted in the accumulation of\ncash advances by AOs, which overstated the\nReceivable accounts and understated the related\nExpense accounts as of December 31, 2024.\nAudit Recommendations\nb.Ensure that O&E who will retire, resign or\ntransfer to other agencies settle their\naccountabilities before issuing them clearance\ncertificates. Ascertain the actual employment\nstatus of those with no information as to whether\nthey are still active or already separated from the\nservice; and\nc.Refrain from granting additional CAs to O&E\nwithout first liquidating their previous CAs\npursuant to Section 4.1.2 of COA Circular No. 97-\n002 dated February 10, 1997.\nAAR 2024\nObservation No. 3\nPage 87\n3.\nThe accuracy, existence and completeness of\nvarious receivables accounts as of December 31,\n2024, cannot be ascertained due to the following:\na.\nReceivables totaling P276.143 million were\nrecorded in total amount without SL details or\nsupporting documentation to substantiate the\ncomposition of the balances;\nb.\nUnsupported balances of Inter-Agency\nReceivables amounting to P23.682 million;\n3.24. We recommended that Management\nrequire:\na. The OCAT to:\nMaintain SLs for all receivable accounts to\nensure that detailed records support the bulk\namounts reflected in the financial statements.\nImmediately coordinate and reconcile with the\nconcerned NGAs and GOCCs to confirm the\nJunconfirmed balances and establish the correct\namount for the affected accounts.\nPrepare adjusting entries to correct\nmisstatements identified upon thorough\nevaluation of the transactions\nAction Plan\nAGENCY ACTION PLAN\nPerson/Dept.\nResponsible\nTarget Implementation Date\nStatus of\nImplementation\nFrom\nTo\nReason for Partial/Delay/\nNon-Implementation, if\napplicable\nAction Taken/Action to\nbe Taken\nThe MUSO undertake to faithfully submit\na complete and up-to-date schedule of\nreceivables, including collections and\nageing reports pertaining to Land-for-the-\nLandless Program, to OCAT on a timely\nbasis.\nOCAT\nPage 2 of 24\n",
